      "readme_excerpt": "The is a debugger for error traces. is a model checker for C. CBMC will explore all possible paths through your code on all possible inputs, and will check that all assertions in your code are true. CBMC can also check for the possibility of security issues (like buffer overflow) and for instances of undefined behavior (like signed integer overflow). If CBMC finds a code issue, it generates an error trace demonstrating how that issue could occur. If CBMC terminates without finding any issues, the result is assurance that your code behaves as expected. CBMC is a *bounded* model checker,",
